"""gen.py a n N [--sb] [--assume WORD] > out.cnf
CNF: there is a cyclic partial word u of length N over {0..a-1, *} such that
every word w in {0..a-1}^n is covered by exactly one window u_i..u_{i+n-1} (indices mod N).
No structural lemma is assumed (diamond periodicity, frames, etc. are NOT encoded).
Vars: L(p,c) [1-based] = "position p holds letter c"; no letter at p means a diamond.
      C(i,w) <-> window i covers word w  <->  AND_j AND_{c != w_j} not L(i+j,c).
--sb : unit clause C(0,0^n) (rotation normalisation: some window covers 0^n; rotate it to 0).
--assume U : unit clauses fixing u to the string U (chars 0-9 or '*'); used for known-answer gates.
"""
